  ('4032NLP6X', 'Students learn core natural language processing techniques at the intersection of computer science, linguistics and AI, with attention to modern language technologies.'),
  ('4343ADVDX', 'Students learn modern data mining methods for massive datasets, including streaming data, similarity search, anomaly detection, clustering, recommender systems and dimensionality reduction.'),
  ('4343AIART', 'This course combines generative AI techniques with critical reflection on creativity, authorship, aesthetics, ethics and the changing role of machines in artistic practice.'),
  ('4343AISOC', 'Students examine AI through social, political, ethical and environmental lenses, then apply these perspectives to real domains through a speculative hands-on project.'),
  ('4343APQALY', 'An advanced quantum computing course focused on practical algorithm design for chemistry, physics, machine learning and the error correction methods needed for noisy devices.'),
  ('4343AUDIO', 'This seminar covers speech recognition, audio synthesis and content-based audio retrieval through lectures, workshops, literature study, student presentations and final project demos.'),
  ('4343AUTMX', 'Students study how AutoML selects algorithms and tunes hyperparameters so machine learning systems can achieve strong predictive performance on new datasets.'),
  ('4343BAYOP', 'This course teaches Bayesian optimization for expensive black-box functions, covering Gaussian processes, acquisition functions, noisy observations, constraints and practical Python applications.'),
  ('4343BICAI', 'Students investigate efficient AI inspired by the brain, including compression, quantization, neuromorphic computing and hardware approaches for low-power machine learning.'),
  ('4343BIOMD', 'Students model biological processes with formal computational frameworks such as Boolean networks and Petri nets, combining lectures, tool practice and interdisciplinary project work.'),
  ('4343BSCC4', 'Second-year students apply earlier business and IT knowledge to real or realistic company cases, analyzing problems and presenting practical recommendations to management.'),
  ('4343BSCSM', 'A management-oriented cybersecurity course for future CIOs, covering organizational risk, governance, policy and the business impact of ICT security decisions.'),
  ('4343BSDPM', 'Students examine how governments use data for policy, focusing on digital-era governance, data readiness, infrastructure, accountability and technology-driven public innovation.'),
  ('4343BSEA6', 'Students learn enterprise architecture methods and models for designing coherent organizations, aligning business processes, information systems, principles and implementation choices.'),
  ('4343BSGBG', 'Students are introduced to company management through a CIO-focused simulation game that connects business decisions, ICT strategy and organizational consequences.'),
  ('4343BSICT', 'Students examine how ICT transforms organizational processes, focusing on process thinking, innovation and the redesign of business activities through information technologies.'),
  ('4343BSMAC', 'Second-year Business Studies students prepare for internships and thesis work, covering research topics, host organizations, supervision, project execution and thesis expectations.'),
  ('4343BSMDS', 'Students learn conceptual modeling and model-driven engineering for large enterprise information systems, covering modeling notations, principles, tools and implementation approaches.'),
  ('4343BSMLB', 'Students learn how machine learning supports business analytics, turning organizational data into predictive insights for decisions in business and government contexts.'),
  ('4343BSMSE', 'Students examine why software becomes costly to evolve, studying maintenance, legacy systems, technical debt and strategies for managing long-term software change.'),
