  ('4343BSSDP', 'Students learn software product management and development, covering product strategy, lifecycle management, Scrum, project planning, quality, risk and user expectations.'),
  ('4343CICSX', 'Students learn causal inference for machine learning, using structural causal models, potential outcomes, interventions, counterfactuals and data-driven causal discovery methods.'),
  ('4343CIMTO', 'This seminar introduces computational imaging and tomography, connecting physical measurement models, inverse problems, algorithms, high-performance computing and advanced research literature.'),
  ('4343CLCMX', 'This course surveys cloud computing from infrastructure and deployment models to scalability, resource management, cloud programming, research papers and hands-on platform assignments.'),
  ('4343CMS6X', 'Students study computational models and programming language semantics, using functional, probabilistic and categorical perspectives alongside Haskell assignments and a research project.'),
  ('4343CRYPE', 'Students study secure implementation of cryptographic algorithms in hardware and software, considering design constraints such as performance, resources, energy use and side-channel risks.'),
  ('4343DASPR', 'Students work on real Fieldlab data problems, moving from problem exploration and data quality assessment to solution design and applied data science practice.'),
  ('4343DDORW', 'Students model and solve real-world optimization problems with constraints, uncertainty and data, connecting theoretical foundations to practical decision-making applications.'),
  ('4343DISYX', 'This course covers the principles behind distributed systems that power social networks, government services and streaming platforms, with attention to reliability and coordination.'),
  ('4343EMBSS', 'Students study embedded systems that interact tightly with physical environments, from appliances and medical devices to portable systems, with focus on architecture and software constraints.'),
  ('4343EVALX', 'Students study evolutionary algorithms that search for solutions through population-based variation and selection, applying evolutionary computation to complex optimization problems.'),
  ('4343FSWT6', 'This course teaches software testing foundations, focusing on why faults arise, how testing reveals failures and how systematic techniques improve software reliability.'),
  ('4343HIPX6', 'Students learn high-performance computing concepts, including supercomputer architectures, distributed and shared-memory programming, GPU optimization and performance-aware scientific computing.'),
  ('4343INDLX', 'This course introduces neural network concepts, deep learning architectures and computer vision applications, combining theory with practical understanding of modern deep models.'),
  ('4343INFRX', 'Students study search and information access technologies, from classical retrieval models to modern large language model contexts and practical retrieval challenges.'),
  ('4343IRPRJ', 'Students complete a smaller research project in bioinformatics, gaining experience with scientific research, project planning, innovation and reporting before the master thesis.'),
  ('4343ITDM6', 'Students learn principled approaches for discovering structure in data, focusing on information-theoretic models, exploratory data mining and interpretable pattern discovery.'),
  ('4343MACLA', 'A mandatory thesis-support course where Computer Science students discuss research progress, academic practice and thesis-related topics during regular master class meetings.'),
