  ('4343MMEBX', 'Students learn multimodal modeling for biodiversity monitoring, combining images, audio and biological measurements to improve automated ecological analysis systems.'),
  ('4343MMSY6', 'ACS students study multimedia systems across storage, processing, transmission and presentation of media, connecting system design with practical multimedia applications.'),
  ('4343MOADX', 'Students learn advanced optimization for problems with constraints and multiple objectives, combining computational methods with decision analysis and applied mathematics.'),
  ('4343MRP22', 'Students complete the final thesis project for Computer Science and Business Studies, combining original research with a business research internship.'),
  ('4343MRP30', 'Students complete an original Computer Science thesis project for the Education or Science Communication tracks, contributing research under academic supervision.'),
  ('4343MRP42', 'Students complete the main Computer Science thesis project, conducting original supervised research that forms the final stage of the MSc programme.'),
  ('4343NLPSG', 'Students study NLP methods for socially relevant applications, examining how language technologies can support communication, access and analysis in public-interest domains.'),
  ('4343PROFX', 'Students learn how mathematical proofs can be represented and checked by machines, studying formal proof systems and proof assistants for reliable reasoning.'),
  ('4343QUALG', 'Students study quantum computation and key quantum algorithms, learning how this model differs from classical computing and where it may offer advantages.'),
  ('4343RECSX', 'Students learn how AI-driven recommender systems model user preferences, personalize choices and raise practical issues around data, algorithms, evaluation and impact.'),
  ('4343RINLX', 'Students learn reinforcement learning theory and algorithms, with attention to deep reinforcement learning successes in games, robotics and sequential decision-making problems.'),
  ('4343ROBO6', 'Students study modern robot architectures, sensors, actuators, navigation, mapping, manipulation, human-robot interaction and adaptive behavior in natural environments.'),
